## 2. Pipeline overview

```
                 ┌─────────────┐
   paper ──▶ (1,2) Plan  ──▶ (3) Codebase ──▶ (5,5.1,6,8.2) Codebase ──▶ (7,8,8.1) Iteratively ──▶ (9a,9b,10) Codebase
                 blueprints      repo born      + dataset runner            -fixed codebase           in Docker
                 (no code)       all files      data/metrics/baselines      in-place repair           tests + container
                                 written        wired (stubs)               (content rewrite)         (package only)

         side artifacts:  plan/analysis     —     eval_plan.json   rubric.json    test_specs.json   task.toml/Dockerfile
```
**Figure 1.** The five phase-groups. Boxes are repository states $R_i$; the bottom row lists the side artifact each stage emits. Two of the five stages (*Plan*, the rubric half of *Repair*) emit only side artifacts; the rest mutate the repository.

A useful coarse distinction (formalized per-stage in Section 3 and summarized in Table 1) is between three mutation types:

- **CREATE** — files that did not exist are written (structure appears).
- **REWRITE** — existing files are edited in place (behavior changes, structure stable).
- **PACKAGE / SPEC** — the repository source is untouched; the stage emits a side artifact or wraps the repo.

| Stage (phases) | Primary mutation | What appears in the repo | Side artifact emitted |
|---|---|---|---|
| Plan (1, 2) | SPEC | — (nothing yet) | plan, architecture, per-file analysis, config template |
| Codebase (3) | **CREATE** | entire source tree, deps, config | coding traces |
| + Dataset runner (5, 5.1, 6, 8.2) | **CREATE** | data-prep, metrics, dataset/baseline configs, baseline-runner modules (stubs), downloaded assets | `eval_plan.json` (datasets/baselines + feasibility) |
| Iteratively-fixed (7, 8, 8.1) | **REWRITE** | (no new source files; backups only) | reproduction rubric + Paper2Code rubric tree |
| In Docker (9a, 9b, 10) | CREATE (tests) + PACKAGE | unit-test suite, then container bundle | `test_specs.json`, `task.toml`, `Dockerfile` |

**Table 1.** Per-stage mutation type and emitted artifacts. Only two stages create *behavioral* source structure (Codebase, Dataset runner); the Repair stage is structurally stable by design.

