## 5. Quantitative analysis

All figures below were obtained directly from the two snapshots with `diff -rq`, `find`, and `wc -l`, and are re-checkable via the commands in the file header.

| Metric | Stage 3 (post-synthesis) | Stage 8.1 (post-repair) | Δ |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Source files (`.py/.yaml/.md/.sh`, excl. backups/caches) | 164 | 164 | **0** |
| Python LOC | 51,049 | 51,223 | +174 |
| Net source lines (all changed text files) | — | — | **+415 / −163  (net +252)** |
| Source files edited in place | — | 15 | 15 |
| Non-destructive backups added (`.bak`) | 0 | 16 | +16 |
| Grading-only artifacts changed (`eval/*.json`, not code) | — | 4 | (excluded from code totals) |

**Table 2.** Stage 3 → Stage 8.1 repository delta. The defining observation: **the file count does not change and no net source files are added** — the repair stage is content-rewriting, not structure-adding. (The four `eval/*.json` changes are grader outputs, not source, and are excluded from code totals.)

| Edited file | + | − | Nature of change |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| `configs/datasets.yaml` | 129 | 53 | collection → per-task; `eval`→`test`; paper-scale sizes (Listing 6) |
| `src/diffusion/guidance.py` | 35 | 9 | implement optional self-recurrence refinement (Listing 7) |
| `src/baselines/nle.py` | 27 | 8 | stub → faithful `sbi` NLE (Listing 4) |
| `src/baselines/{npe,npse,nre}.py` | (similar) | | stub → faithful `sbi` implementations |
| `scripts/prepare_data.py` | — | — | download-budget tracking; explicit `test_num_samples` |
| `config.yaml` | 1 | 0 | add paper-mandated `training_simulations: 100000` (Listing 5) |
| `tests/test_data_prep.py` | — | — | assertions updated to per-task layout |

**Table 3.** Per-file deltas for the most significant edits (verified). The largest change is configuration realignment, not new algorithms — consistent with the thesis that structure is set early and repair *tunes* it.

**Interpretation.** Three quantitative signatures distinguish the repair stage from the creation stages: (i) zero change in file count; (ii) a small net line delta (+252) dominated by a single config refactor; and (iii) one backup per edited file. Together they confirm that, in this pipeline, *behavioral fidelity is achieved by rewriting a stable set of files*, not by regenerating the repository.

